# Laravel Backend Rules

## Structure

- Controllers: `app/Http/Controllers/` with subdirs (`Auth/`, `Settings/`, `DevTools/`)
- Form requests: `app/Http/Requests/` for validation-heavy forms
- Models: `app/Models/` — keep accessors/mutators on the model

## Controllers

- Return `Inertia::render('path/to/page')` for pages
- Return `response()->json([...])` for dev-tool API endpoints
- Validate inline or via `$request->validate([...])` for simple JSON APIs
- Use `ValidationException::withMessages()` for domain validation errors

## Routes (`routes/web.php`)

```php
Route::get('dev-tools/example', function () {
    return Inertia::render('dev-tools/example');
})->name('dev-tools.example');
```

For server-backed tools, use a dedicated controller:

```php
Route::get('dev-tools/hash-generator', [HashGeneratorController::class, 'show'])
    ->name('dev-tools.hash-generator');
Route::post('dev-tools/hash-generator/bcrypt', [HashGeneratorController::class, 'bcrypt'])
    ->name('dev-tools.hash-generator.bcrypt');
```

## User model

Extended fields: `role`, `title`, `avatar_seed`, `bio`. Accessors: `avatar_url`, `is_admin`.

## Shared Inertia data

`HandleInertiaRequests` shares `auth.user` (with appended `avatar_url`, `is_admin`), `name`, `quote`. Do not break this contract.

## PHPUnit tests

- Location: `tests/Feature/`, `tests/Unit/`
- Use `RefreshDatabase` when touching DB
- Page tests: `assertInertia(fn (Assert $page) => $page->component('dev-tools/foo'))`
- API tests: `postJson(route('...'))->assertOk()->assertJson([...])`
- Data providers: `#[DataProvider('methodName')]` (see `DevToolsRoutesTest`)

## Formatting

Run `vendor/bin/pint` before committing PHP changes.
